        </p>

        <h2 style="color: #003853; font-size: 1.8rem; font-family: var(--font-display, serif); margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">1. Which Safari Park Should You Choose from Zanzibar?</h2>
        <p>Choosing the right park depends entirely on your available vacation days, budget, and which specific animals sit atop your wishlist:</p>

        <!-- MIKUMI CARD -->
        <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8ed; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <h3 style="color: #003853; font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 0;">A. Mikumi National Park — Best for 1-Day Fly-In (No Overnights)</h3>
            <span style="font-weight: 700; color: #0284c7;">Flight: 45–55 mins direct • From $440/pax</span>
          </div>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569;">
            Mikumi is the most popular island add-on because it requires zero nights away from your resort. You board a morning turboprop plane at 07:00, land directly on Mikumi's Kikoboga dirt airstrip, embark on a 6-hour open-roof 4x4 game drive across the Mkata Floodplain, enjoy a hot bush lunch, and fly back at 16:00 in time for dinner on Zanzibar.
          </p>
          <div style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #0f172a; background: #fff; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;">
            <strong>Wildlife Reality Check:</strong> Excellent for lions, elephants, Cape buffaloes, giraffes, and hippos. <em>Note: There are zero rhinos in Mikumi.</em>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SERENGETI CARD -->
        <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8ed; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <h3 style="color: #003853; font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 0;">B. Serengeti National Park — The Bucket-List 3-Day Fly-In</h3>
            <span style="font-weight: 700; color: #0284c7;">Flight: 1h 45m charter • From $900/pax</span>
          </div>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569;">
            The crown jewel of African wildlife. Fly directly to Seronera (central) or Kogatende (north) airstrips. Stay inside the park in a luxury tented camp where game wander freely past camp. Experience the world-famous Great Migration (July–October river crossings in the north; December–March calving season in Ndutu).
          </p>
          <div style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #0f172a; background: #fff; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;">
            <strong>Wildlife Reality Check:</strong> Africa's highest predator density (lions, leopards in trees, cheetahs hunting). All Big Five present (rhinos are rare, confined to Moru Kopjes).
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- NGORONGORO CRATER CARD -->
        <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8ed; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
