            <h3 style="color: #003853; font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 0;">C. Ngorongoro Crater — The Guaranteed Big Five Sanctuary</h3>
            <span style="font-weight: 700; color: #0284c7;">Flight: ZNZ ⇄ Arusha/Lake Manyara + 4x4</span>
          </div>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569;">
            A volcanic caldera 600 meters deep enclosing over 260 square kilometers of lush grassland and soda lakes. Because animals cannot easily leave the caldera, Ngorongoro offers the densest concentration of large mammals on Earth, including over 25,000 animals in a single bowl.
          </p>
          <div style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #0f172a; background: #fff; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;">
            <strong>Wildlife Reality Check:</strong> Best place in East Africa to see the critically endangered <strong>Black Rhinoceros</strong> alongside dense lion prides, flamingos in Lake Magadi, and giant bull elephants.
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 style="color: #003853; font-size: 1.8rem; font-family: var(--font-display, serif); margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">2. The Big Five: Where Can You Actually Spot Them?</h2>
